WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:02.370
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:02.640 --> 01:03.760
[Beast: Answer me]

3
01:05.320 --> 01:08.258
What's going on?

4
01:48.913 --> 01:51.520
That unhinged bastard!

5
01:54.960 --> 01:56.226
[Beast] Just hold on.

6
01:56.226 --> 01:58.986
I'm going home right now to smash the camcorder.

7
01:58.986 --> 02:00.686
Camcorder?

8
02:14.580 --> 02:17.432
If we smash the camcorder now and flee to the future...

9
02:18.093 --> 02:22.876
it still won't change the fact that Yoon Ha Na got kidnapped here, in the past!

10
02:24.200 --> 02:26.177
I'm the only one who can save her...

11
02:26.177 --> 02:27.877
right now.

12
02:52.606 --> 02:54.531
What... is this?

13
02:57.200 --> 03:00.050
Year... 2026?

14
03:04.833 --> 03:07.297
I'm just curious.

15
03:07.297 --> 03:09.614
Why would you quit acting?

16
03:09.614 --> 03:11.171
Jun Mo...

17
03:11.171 --> 03:12.871
Why!

18
03:16.677 --> 03:18.528
I'm asking you.

19
03:21.098 --> 03:24.399
What, in the future you just came back from...

20
03:25.602 --> 03:27.917
Did I kill you or something?

21
03:35.926 --> 03:37.626
Jun Mo, I...

22
03:38.626 --> 03:42.130
I don't think you're making much sense.

23
03:43.706 --> 03:46.010
Do you really think it's so improbable?

24
03:49.553 --> 03:51.726
I think it does make sense.

25
03:51.726 --> 03:53.927
In fact, I'm pretty sure of it.

26
03:54.906 --> 03:58.098
- Jun Mo... - Don't beat around the bush, just tell me.

27
03:59.233 --> 04:00.933
Ha Na!

28
04:19.740 --> 04:22.125
I'm sorry, Ha Na. Are you alright?

29
04:25.026 --> 04:27.800
I-I wasn't in my right mind.

30
04:28.566 --> 04:30.045
Are you okay?

31
04:39.993 --> 04:42.979
Yang Jun Mo, you bastard, where are you?

32
04:48.033 --> 04:49.530
Hello?

33
04:50.400 --> 04:52.100
Yeah, come quickly.

34
04:55.567 --> 04:57.374
[Episode 10]

35
05:04.753 --> 05:06.453
I'm sorry, Ha Na.

36
05:08.600 --> 05:11.330
I just wanted to convince you with my synopsis,

37
05:11.330 --> 05:13.030
but I flew off the handle.

38
05:14.626 --> 05:16.326
The script...

39
05:16.946 --> 05:18.646
What is it?

40
05:19.640 --> 05:21.006
It's a temporary title for now,

41
05:21.006 --> 05:23.490
but it's called "Lost Time."

42
05:23.490 --> 05:25.214
"Lost time?"

43
05:25.214 --> 05:27.965
It's about using an old camcorder to travel back and forth in time.

44
05:27.965 --> 05:32.781
I was stuck on giving the female protagonist a compelling motive to travel back in time,

45
05:32.781 --> 05:35.121
but talking with you gave me a spark of an idea.

46
05:35.740 --> 05:38.539
What if the protagonist died?

47
05:38.539 --> 05:42.956
For the protagonist to have a strong motivation to travel back in time,

48
05:42.956 --> 05:45.307
someone would have to die.

49
05:45.307 --> 05:46.784
That's the idea.

50
05:46.784 --> 05:49.608
The scenario is supposed to be written in 2026.

51
05:49.608 --> 05:52.732
Did my rejection cause it to be written sooner?

52
05:52.732 --> 05:54.432
I've been thinking of you, and only you...

53
05:56.253 --> 05:57.457
What?

54
05:57.457 --> 05:59.861
the whole time I was writing the script.

55
05:59.861 --> 06:02.065
We've been doing so well up until now,

56
06:02.065 --> 06:05.290
and I've never doubted our future for even a second.

57
06:07.102 --> 06:09.073
I'm sorry, Jun Mo.

58
06:09.073 --> 06:10.359
Ha Na.

59
06:11.342 --> 06:13.822
I mean it with all my heart when I say this.

60
06:13.822 --> 06:15.593
I hope you don't give up on acting.

61
06:15.593 --> 06:17.337
You don't have to do my movie.

62
06:17.337 --> 06:19.374
Please, just reconsider it.

63
06:19.374 --> 06:21.625
Just think about whether you, Ha Na,

64
06:21.625 --> 06:24.676
will be able to live a happy life as anything other than an actress.

65
06:27.382 --> 06:29.382
You are...

66
06:29.382 --> 06:31.082
the best actress ever, at least to me.

67
06:31.805 --> 06:33.529
Whatever anyone else says,

68
06:33.529 --> 06:35.666
you are the best ever, at least in my life.

69
06:36.418 --> 06:37.712
Got it?

70
06:46.829 --> 06:48.254
Ha Na!

71
06:49.295 --> 06:51.368
You bastard!

72
06:54.147 --> 06:55.599
Let's go.

73
07:21.089 --> 07:23.265
Are you sure you're okay?

74
07:24.299 --> 07:26.301
Yeah, I'm fine.

75
07:26.301 --> 07:29.296
What can I do to get back to that lunatic?

76
07:31.515 --> 07:33.171
Desperation.

77
07:33.809 --> 07:36.439
Yang Jun Mo's heart was filled with it.

78
07:36.439 --> 07:38.689
What are you going on about now?

79
07:38.689 --> 07:40.785
He was just so desperate...

80
07:42.192 --> 07:44.207
to be good at something.

81
07:46.015 --> 07:48.109
Desperation? Wanting to be good at something?

82
07:48.109 --> 07:50.093
That's not an excuse for his behavior!

83
07:51.822 --> 07:53.815
What he did is just wrong.

84
07:53.815 --> 07:57.049
Don't let pity or sympathy get the better of you.

85
07:57.049 --> 07:58.333
Yoon Ha Na.

86
07:58.333 --> 08:00.245
Pity should be reserved for human beings.

87
08:00.909 --> 08:03.482
Don't waste it on those lesser than human.

88
08:06.174 --> 08:08.549
Can't Jun Mo's future...

89
08:09.262 --> 08:11.619
change, as Hyeong Won's did?

90
08:11.619 --> 08:13.139
Yoon Ha Na.

91
08:15.049 --> 08:18.486
We are, in fact, somehow traveling through time right now,

92
08:18.486 --> 08:20.422
but we're not gods.

93
08:23.582 --> 08:25.742
We...

94
08:25.742 --> 08:28.580
should just stick to doing our best at what we can manage.

95
08:31.015 --> 08:32.391
Okay.

96
08:41.809 --> 08:45.006
First of all, Lee Hyeong Won is on the semi-pro judo team now,

97
08:45.006 --> 08:47.930
so it wouldn't make sense for him to team up with Jun Mo to come for you.

98
08:47.930 --> 08:52.178
Does someone else take up Lee Hyeong Won's role in the narrative, then?

99
08:52.178 --> 08:54.609
Or maybe it just doesn't happen at all.

100
08:55.724 --> 08:57.609
I wish that was the case.

101
08:57.609 --> 09:00.139
Yang Jun Mo is the stalker...

102
09:00.139 --> 09:02.663
Then what's the deal with Lee Hyeong Won?

103
09:02.663 --> 09:04.487
What do they have to do with each other?

104
09:04.487 --> 09:08.278
Besides, didn't he originally disappear during sophomore year?

105
09:08.278 --> 09:11.589
- What could this mean? - Why would they gang up on not only you,

106
09:11.589 --> 09:14.140
but Woo Jae as well? There's no reason to!

107
09:14.822 --> 09:16.900
I have no clue.

108
09:19.089 --> 09:21.329
Should we just go after Lee Hyeong Won first?

109
09:21.329 --> 09:24.709
Apparently, he's best friends with Woo Jae, so you should approach him and...

110
09:27.095 --> 09:28.795
Where have you been?

111
09:30.655 --> 09:33.120
- Woo Jae. - Hey, what are you...

112
09:33.120 --> 09:35.083
What were you doing here?

113
09:35.083 --> 09:37.047
Ha Na wasn't picking up my calls.

114
09:37.047 --> 09:40.857
My schedule got canceled, so I came by to see you, Ha Na.

115
09:41.891 --> 09:44.749
I lost my phone.

116
09:44.749 --> 09:46.789
What happened? Should we go get a new one?

117
09:46.789 --> 09:49.290
No, no. I want to look for it a bit more.

118
09:51.335 --> 09:53.821
I was thinking we could go on a date near the Han River.

119
09:55.589 --> 09:57.369
Sure.

120
09:57.369 --> 10:00.209
I'm going to the convenience store. Do you want anything?

121
10:00.209 --> 10:01.593
- Nope. - No, thank you.

122
10:01.593 --> 10:02.867
I'll be quick.

123
10:44.329 --> 10:46.355
Concentrate on the movie.

124
10:47.062 --> 10:48.679
I know, but...

125
10:48.679 --> 10:50.323
You're just so pretty.

126
10:50.323 --> 10:52.648
I can't concentrate at all.

127
10:54.142 --> 10:55.842
Stop being silly.

128
11:03.143 --> 11:04.382
My...

129
11:05.001 --> 11:06.379
Saving...

130
11:06.379 --> 11:09.422
"Saving you in my heart!"

131
11:09.422 --> 11:12.315
What on earth did I just witness?

132
11:13.329 --> 11:15.013
You don't know this?

133
11:15.013 --> 11:17.009
It's a trend that's going on.

134
11:17.009 --> 11:20.034
"Saving you in my heart!"

135
11:24.293 --> 11:26.759
That's weird. He said you'd love this.

136
11:26.759 --> 11:29.161
- Who told you that? - Soo Hyuk.

137
11:30.253 --> 11:31.310
Was it a prank?

138
11:31.310 --> 11:33.585
I'm going to give him a piece of my mind.

139
11:34.479 --> 11:37.381
"Saving you in my heart!"

140
11:38.019 --> 11:40.786
- Stop that. - "Saving!"

141
11:40.786 --> 11:42.486
You're adorable.

142
11:47.062 --> 11:48.453
I'm sorry.

143
11:48.453 --> 11:51.846
Sorry that we can't leave the car, let alone go to the movies.

144
11:51.846 --> 11:53.271
Whatever.

145
11:53.271 --> 11:57.279
I prefer being alone with you over being in a crowded movie theater.

146
11:57.279 --> 11:59.819
See? We can hold hands, judgment-free!

147
11:59.819 --> 12:01.519
I absolutely love it.

148
12:02.419 --> 12:03.892
Thank you.

149
12:06.957 --> 12:08.550
Woo Jae.

150
12:08.550 --> 12:09.887
Yes?

151
12:09.887 --> 12:11.587
You know, I...

152
12:13.073 --> 12:16.313
I hope you live a happy life, Woo Jae.

153
12:16.313 --> 12:18.813
And a long one at that.

154
12:20.639 --> 12:24.083
Well, I am really happy right now.

155
12:25.934 --> 12:27.384
Me too.

156
12:34.666 --> 12:36.102
Woo Jae.

157
12:37.373 --> 12:39.326
If...

158
12:39.326 --> 12:41.573
Hypothetically speaking...

159
12:43.839 --> 12:47.237
Imagine we broke up in a really bad way.

160
12:50.873 --> 12:53.275
I don't see that happening, but...

161
12:53.933 --> 12:55.475
Okay, if so, then what?

162
12:56.559 --> 12:58.259
I will...

163
12:59.719 --> 13:02.169
wish you happiness with all my heart

164
13:02.804 --> 13:05.060
wherever you end up without me,

165
13:05.666 --> 13:08.573
and whoever you end up with. Even if it isn't me.

166
13:11.873 --> 13:13.573
For me...

167
13:15.333 --> 13:18.922
the fact that I can love you with everything I have...

168
13:19.913 --> 13:21.768
just gives me so much joy.

169
13:23.179 --> 13:25.145
It makes me happy.

170
13:30.259 --> 13:33.128
Ha Na. I need to ask you this.

171
13:34.187 --> 13:36.823
Did you refuse to star in Director Yang Jun Mo's film...

172
13:36.823 --> 13:38.936
because of me?

173
13:38.936 --> 13:40.760
Because I didn't want you to?

174
13:40.760 --> 13:44.610
The script wasn't all made up.

175
13:46.656 --> 13:50.528
No, I just made a decision after thinking long and hard about it.

176
13:52.976 --> 13:54.353
Woo Jae.

177
13:54.353 --> 13:56.631
Could you tell me...

178
13:56.631 --> 14:00.590
why you hate Jun Mo so much?

179
14:03.563 --> 14:06.313
- That's... - I'm just curious.

180
14:11.369 --> 14:13.373
Truth be told,

181
14:13.373 --> 14:16.495
I saw something strange.

182
14:34.030 --> 14:36.489
"My little canary...

183
14:36.489 --> 14:38.202
who stole my soul?"

184
14:40.149 --> 14:42.003
"Slit its throat..."

185
14:42.927 --> 14:45.829
[My sweetheart shines brightly on the monitor. Should I behead you and hold a funeral?]

186
14:45.829 --> 14:47.093
"My sweetheart, on the monitor..."

187
14:47.093 --> 14:48.777
Get the ones out in the front, first.

188
14:48.777 --> 14:50.488
- Yes, sir. - Good, good.

189
14:53.407 --> 14:54.413
[50th class, Yang Jun Mo]

190
14:55.503 --> 14:58.623
The sweetheart on Jun Mo's monitor would be...

191
14:59.709 --> 15:01.409
What's up, Woo Jae?

192
15:11.463 --> 15:12.934
Woo Jae.

193
15:14.229 --> 15:16.474
Stay in your lane.

194
15:20.956 --> 15:24.083
It dropped out of the bag I was trying to pack.

195
15:28.169 --> 15:30.687
It's a little bit embarrassing, you know.

196
15:30.687 --> 15:34.324
I just scribble down whatever idea comes to mind.

197
15:34.324 --> 15:37.081
A lot of these end up in parts of my scenarios,

198
15:37.081 --> 15:39.806
so I hope you understand that I can't help but be secretive about it.

199
15:40.929 --> 15:42.629
Yes.

200
15:42.629 --> 15:44.286
Jun Mo!

201
15:44.286 --> 15:46.203
- Are you coming? - Yeah.

202
15:48.043 --> 15:50.758
- I have to go. See you later. - Sure.

203
16:02.196 --> 16:03.896
Hey, Soo Hyuk!

204
16:07.976 --> 16:10.313
- Here, the pillows you asked for! - Thank you.

205
16:10.313 --> 16:12.956
- Here you go! - Thank you!

206
16:12.956 --> 16:14.380
We'll get going now.

207
16:14.380 --> 16:16.862
- Yeah, good job today! - Good night.

208
16:17.556 --> 16:20.560
Director Yang, you can sleep in my room. It's pretty crowded out here.

209
16:20.560 --> 16:22.084
Thank you.

210
16:22.084 --> 16:23.784
Hey, hey, Ha Ru!

211
16:25.656 --> 16:27.735
Our day is far from over.

212
16:28.359 --> 16:31.763
We need to talk about the correlation between world-building and range.

213
16:31.763 --> 16:34.444
- Over there, I assume? - I thought we just did that!

214
16:34.444 --> 16:36.163
But I already understood everything...

215
16:36.163 --> 16:38.264
There he goes again...

216
16:41.782 --> 16:43.483
Ye Rang, aren't you going to sleep?

217
16:43.483 --> 16:46.106
I just need to wrap up. You go to bed first.

218
16:49.422 --> 16:51.001
Good night!

219
17:09.949 --> 17:13.551
Stop loitering behind my back and say what you want to say.

220
17:16.808 --> 17:18.679
Do you know...

221
17:18.679 --> 17:22.731
when Ha Na started working on Director Jun Mo's film?

222
17:22.731 --> 17:25.301
June 5th, 2012.

223
17:27.009 --> 17:31.475
No need to be surprised. It's just a day I'll never forget.

224
17:31.475 --> 17:35.895
That was the day of the first audition that Ha Na took for Jun Mo's films.

225
17:35.895 --> 17:38.586
Ha Na ended up being the female lead,

226
17:38.586 --> 17:41.090
and signaled the start of Seo Ye Rang's inability to secure a lead role.

227
17:41.090 --> 17:43.295
That's June 5th, 2012.

228
17:43.990 --> 17:46.161
So, why are you asking?

229
17:48.030 --> 17:49.537
It's nothing.

230
17:55.457 --> 17:57.830
[My little canary, who stole my soul. You are what completes me.]

231
18:12.957 --> 18:14.532
Hey, Yoon Ha Na...

232
18:16.690 --> 18:18.390
What a sight.

233
18:20.597 --> 18:22.530
- What are they doing? - Look at those lovebirds!

234
18:24.977 --> 18:27.181
- Let's go. Move! - Move, move!

235
18:30.464 --> 18:31.844
Let's go!

236
18:32.630 --> 18:34.330
Yeah, let's go.

237
18:35.883 --> 18:38.121
Once I saw it,

238
18:38.121 --> 18:40.377
I couldn't stop noticing it.

239
18:40.377 --> 18:43.923
He'd get this beady look in his eyes every time he saw you, Ha Na.

240
18:44.530 --> 18:47.857
What, in the future you just came back from...

241
18:48.887 --> 18:50.944
Did I kill you or something?

242
18:50.944 --> 18:53.517
I'm sorry, Ha Na. Are you alright?

243
18:56.140 --> 18:58.757
I-I wasn't in my right mind.

244
18:59.433 --> 19:01.924
So, Woo Jae was the first to witness...

245
19:01.924 --> 19:04.061
Jun Mo's true face.

246
19:04.061 --> 19:05.885
Ha Na.

247
19:05.885 --> 19:07.689
Do you think...

248
19:07.689 --> 19:11.653
I've become that type of guy who gets jealous and ruins his talented girlfriend's future?

249
19:11.653 --> 19:13.930
Is that who I am now?

250
19:14.680 --> 19:16.671
No, you're not.

251
19:16.671 --> 19:22.329
Your talented girlfriend doesn't need Jun Mo to have a good future.

252
19:22.329 --> 19:24.029
So stop worrying.

253
19:57.899 --> 19:59.415
Woo Jae.

254
20:00.726 --> 20:02.717
You know, I...

255
20:02.717 --> 20:05.566
I hope you live a happy life, Woo Jae.

256
20:06.386 --> 20:09.201
And a long one at that.

257
20:13.019 --> 20:15.741
Ha Na. I need to ask you this.

258
20:16.958 --> 20:19.637
Did you refuse to star in Director Yang Jun Mo's film...

259
20:20.759 --> 20:22.459
because of me?

260
20:23.299 --> 20:25.004
Because I didn't want you to?

261
20:41.243 --> 20:43.673
You know I'm good friends with Reporter Yang.

262
20:43.673 --> 20:48.416
I got a tip that some journalists from ThisTrue will be raking through the whole Han River.

263
20:48.416 --> 20:50.837
So I came running right away.

264
20:51.516 --> 20:55.913
How's this? "Ye Rang Entertainment's employees gather for a bonding meeting at the Han River."

265
20:55.913 --> 20:59.349
We're sorry to inconvenience you, Ye Rang.

266
20:59.349 --> 21:00.987
Thank you, Ye Rang.

267
21:00.987 --> 21:03.944
No need. I'm glad to be here.

268
21:03.944 --> 21:06.315
I'm on a date, too, so...

269
21:06.315 --> 21:10.271
I haven't seen him in a while, you know.

270
21:13.536 --> 21:14.867
Really?

271
21:14.867 --> 21:17.425
I... don't recall.

272
21:29.529 --> 21:31.579
- Stop stuffing your face. - You can have it.

273
22:19.483 --> 22:21.515
Copycat!

274
22:34.949 --> 22:39.300
I need to tell her that I'm quitting.

275
22:46.469 --> 22:49.120
Is everything okay, Ye Rang?

276
22:49.120 --> 22:50.269
Huh?

277
22:54.329 --> 22:55.736
Well...

278
22:56.949 --> 22:59.520
This isn't about me,

279
22:59.520 --> 23:02.460
but a friend of a friend of mine...

280
23:04.169 --> 23:06.437
A friend of a friend, you say?

281
23:07.543 --> 23:08.567
What is it?

282
23:08.567 --> 23:10.026
[The Hannam, Chef Mun]

283
23:23.003 --> 23:26.240
Hey, by the way, is Ha Na okay?

284
23:27.636 --> 23:31.285
- What do you mean? - She turned Director Yang Jun Mo down, right?

285
23:31.969 --> 23:34.303
Don't even mention that lunatic, Yang Jun Mo!

286
23:34.303 --> 23:37.216
He went all "Fast &amp; Furious" with Ha Na, and I had to...

287
23:37.216 --> 23:38.900
What did you just say?

288
23:38.900 --> 23:41.253
Yang Jun Mo did what with Ha Na?

289
23:43.136 --> 23:44.682
I mean...

290
23:45.656 --> 23:48.096
Her boyfriend is too busy.

291
23:49.249 --> 23:51.618
She waited, and waited...

292
23:53.169 --> 23:55.094
until she grew tired of waiting.

293
23:56.683 --> 23:59.494
She feels like her love is one-sided.

294
24:02.816 --> 24:04.540
She's sad and lonely.

295
24:04.540 --> 24:05.793
Very.

296
24:07.468 --> 24:09.403
Sounds like a joke of a boyfriend.

297
24:09.403 --> 24:12.213
Who does he think he is, making his girlfriend feel lonely?

298
24:18.636 --> 24:22.201
If they're letting the present slip away because of the future...

299
24:23.276 --> 24:25.394
it's not really love, is it?

300
24:28.049 --> 24:31.785
So, Yang Jun Mo did that, huh?

301
24:31.785 --> 24:33.063
Yeah.

302
24:33.063 --> 24:36.796
Yoon Ha Na told me not to tell you because you'd get worried, but...

303
24:38.208 --> 24:40.153
I'll pretend I didn't hear that. But...

304
24:40.153 --> 24:43.156
you need to tell me if anything happens to Ha Na.

305
24:43.156 --> 24:45.429
Yeah, of course!

306
25:03.276 --> 25:05.760
- Are you alright? - Me?

307
25:05.760 --> 25:07.143
What about me?

308
25:07.143 --> 25:09.633
- Are you dense? - Why?

309
25:09.633 --> 25:11.980
Am... I dense?

310
25:12.903 --> 25:16.390
When's the last time you and Ye Rang went on a proper date?

311
25:18.623 --> 25:20.343
I'm not sure.

312
25:20.343 --> 25:23.796
I guess Yoon Ha Ru isn't just dense, but a lost cause as well.

313
25:23.796 --> 25:25.903
What do you mean by that?

314
25:25.903 --> 25:29.423
Don't let your cherished one get away.

315
25:29.423 --> 25:31.373
I'm not exactly planning to.

316
25:31.373 --> 25:32.909
When you're blinded by purpose,

317
25:32.909 --> 25:35.954
you might lose sight of what really matters.

318
25:36.576 --> 25:39.027
I can see my cherished one clear as day!

319
25:39.027 --> 25:40.804
- Crystal clear! - Okay.

320
25:40.804 --> 25:42.756
Good for you.

321
25:42.756 --> 25:44.997
- Let's go. - Aren't you playing?

322
25:45.589 --> 25:47.909
- Come on, one more round! - I said no.

323
25:47.909 --> 25:50.342
- Scared of losing? - I'm not playing.

324
25:58.109 --> 25:59.907
- Are you done playing? - Yeah.

325
25:59.907 --> 26:02.267
- I won! - Really?

326
27:48.049 --> 27:50.940
- Who is it? - Delivery for Yoon Ha Na.

327
27:50.940 --> 27:53.521
What? One minute!

328
28:01.503 --> 28:03.969
- I'm going out. - Okay.

329
28:03.969 --> 28:06.445
- You're going out, too? - I've got a delivery.

330
28:16.041 --> 28:18.202
Nothing to do...

331
28:20.696 --> 28:21.543
[Jung Woo Jae]

332
28:25.435 --> 28:27.854
Yes, it's me. Are you bored?

333
28:27.854 --> 28:30.108
What? No, I'm on the set.

334
28:32.109 --> 28:33.151
What is it?

335
28:33.151 --> 28:35.357
I might be a little paranoid,

336
28:35.357 --> 28:37.541
but could you go to the shared house for me?

337
28:37.541 --> 28:39.408
Isn't Yoon Ha Na there?

338
28:39.408 --> 28:41.904
Why? Is something wrong?

339
28:41.904 --> 28:43.993
Not particularly.

340
28:43.993 --> 28:46.147
Come on, help me out.

341
28:47.109 --> 28:50.013
But it's my three days off.

342
28:50.013 --> 28:52.951
Is it really a good idea to make me protect my best friend's girlfriend

343
28:52.951 --> 28:55.281
who also happens to be my first love, who so brutally turned me down?

344
28:56.909 --> 28:58.800
I did an advertisement for Ike yesterday.

345
28:58.800 --> 29:01.097
They gifted me a... what was it again?

346
29:01.097 --> 29:03.201
An off-black Ike Jordan?

347
29:03.201 --> 29:05.052
- What the hell? - It's a limited edition,

348
29:05.052 --> 29:06.709
so money can't buy it, or so I've heard.

349
29:06.709 --> 29:09.189
- What size? - 285.

350
29:09.189 --> 29:10.419
Deal?

351
29:11.940 --> 29:14.538
Deal. You sly bastard.

352
29:27.963 --> 29:30.335
What's this? Do you think Woo Jae sent this?

353
29:30.335 --> 29:32.035
Is this some kind of surprise?

354
29:43.555 --> 29:45.704
Which sick bastard did this?

355
29:51.056 --> 29:52.363
Hey...

356
29:56.119 --> 29:57.691
You there!

357
30:09.573 --> 30:11.040
Hey.

358
30:14.013 --> 30:15.713
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru!

359
30:18.632 --> 30:20.280
Are you okay?

360
30:21.051 --> 30:22.399
Wait here.

361
30:28.473 --> 30:29.922
Hey, Lee Hyeong Won!

362
30:29.922 --> 30:31.563
Get that bastard!

363
30:31.563 --> 30:32.946
Who?

364
30:44.293 --> 30:45.993
You maniac!

365
30:53.259 --> 30:55.989
Good to see you again, Lee Hyeong Won.

366
31:16.533 --> 31:18.233
Hey, Lee Hyeong Won!

367
31:23.599 --> 31:25.502
Hello, emergency services?

368
31:26.145 --> 31:28.321
Someone's been injured!

369
31:53.313 --> 31:55.097
They said that, with proper treatment and rehabilitation,

370
31:55.097 --> 31:57.733
he'll recover by the end of the year.

371
31:57.733 --> 32:01.299
He'll be okay. He has Woo Jae with him,

372
32:01.299 --> 32:03.415
and his team will take care of him.

373
32:06.686 --> 32:09.186
That would've originally been Lee Hyeong Won,

374
32:09.186 --> 32:11.613
but someone else took his place in the narrative.

375
32:11.613 --> 32:15.232
Lee Hyeong Won, on the other hand, got injured because of us.

376
32:18.543 --> 32:20.253
Jun Mo...

377
32:20.253 --> 32:22.439
If I hadn't turned his movie pitch down,

378
32:22.439 --> 32:26.246
he would've still been a good mentor, and a good director.

379
32:26.246 --> 32:28.059
It's because I turned him down.

380
32:28.059 --> 32:30.819
I made him reveal his true colors sooner.

381
32:30.819 --> 32:32.307
No.

382
32:32.307 --> 32:35.569
He's always been a horrible guy. It just came to light faster than before.

383
32:36.687 --> 32:39.332
The fragments of the past that we twisted have stacked up

384
32:39.332 --> 32:42.322
and introduced too many unpredictable variables.

385
32:42.322 --> 32:44.810
Someone even got hurt.

386
32:47.139 --> 32:49.697
Get it together, Yoon Ha Na.

387
32:49.697 --> 32:52.494
Yes, things have gone wrong, and yes, there are more variables,

388
32:52.494 --> 32:54.754
but everything that should happen has happened.

389
32:55.666 --> 32:56.781
Everything that should happen?

390
32:56.781 --> 32:58.066
You can't even cry!

391
32:58.066 --> 33:00.150
The unrelenting stalking...

392
33:01.039 --> 33:03.048
has started, just like it should.

393
33:05.632 --> 33:08.537
I am sorry about Lee Hyeong Won.

394
33:08.537 --> 33:10.607
But this variable is giving us an advantage.

395
33:10.607 --> 33:13.045
He even went ahead and made a mistake!

396
33:13.045 --> 33:15.889
Every trace that Yang Jun Mo leaves behind from now on

397
33:15.889 --> 33:17.895
is all proof that we can use.

398
33:21.562 --> 33:25.144
He'll... show up again soon, right?

399
33:25.144 --> 33:27.494
We need to prove that Yang Jun Mo is a stalker,

400
33:27.494 --> 33:29.945
and that he hurt someone.

401
33:29.945 --> 33:32.210
It's the only way we'll lock him away for good.

402
33:33.142 --> 33:36.719
Time is on our side now.

403
33:41.442 --> 33:42.934
Lee Hyeong Won...

404
33:50.162 --> 33:51.737
What?

405
33:52.609 --> 33:55.622
So what you're saying is, the bastard who did this to you

406
33:55.622 --> 33:58.150
is someone you know?

407
34:00.309 --> 34:02.540
Who is it? Where does he live?

408
34:02.540 --> 34:05.092
I should go find this bastard and...

409
34:14.876 --> 34:16.576
Who is it?

410
34:18.709 --> 34:20.409
Park Gi Tae.

411
34:21.416 --> 34:23.402
Park Gi Tae?

412
34:23.402 --> 34:26.620
Thank you for lending me your precious time.

413
34:26.620 --> 34:30.876
This here is Jung Woo Jae's updated profile.

414
34:30.876 --> 34:33.566
- He's very handsome. - What a good-looking guy.

415
34:33.566 --> 34:35.330
He's perfect for our newest project.

416
34:35.330 --> 34:36.856
It seems that way.

417
34:36.856 --> 34:40.952
And this is Yoon Ha Na's profile.

418
34:44.314 --> 34:46.786
You know I'm a collector of great actors, right?

419
34:46.786 --> 34:48.790
We know Yoon Ha Na, of course.

420
34:48.790 --> 34:51.008
I enjoyed "The Masked Season."

421
34:51.008 --> 34:54.366
Writer Geum, you must be so busy. How did you find the time to watch it?

422
34:54.366 --> 34:57.582
It's Jeon Hee Ae's work. How could I miss it?

423
34:59.816 --> 35:01.796
Right, of course.

424
35:02.402 --> 35:04.020
CEO Seo.

425
35:04.020 --> 35:05.300
Yes, Ms. Geum?

426
35:05.300 --> 35:08.544
I'll be honest, since it's you.

427
35:08.544 --> 35:12.268
Our new project needs a female lead that's globally recognized.

428
35:12.268 --> 35:14.447
I'm sure you understand.

429
35:15.780 --> 35:17.266
Of course I do.

430
35:17.266 --> 35:21.066
Everyone knows that Yoon Ha Na is a great actress.

431
35:21.066 --> 35:25.062
But she's just too obscure. It's a real shame.

432
35:27.000 --> 35:32.887
Of course, that's why we're working on slowly but surely making her more famous.

433
35:40.313 --> 35:42.045
Thank you for coming by. Safe travels.

434
35:42.045 --> 35:44.113
Let's grab a meal together sometime.

435
35:44.113 --> 35:45.404
- I'd be honored. - Nice seeing you.

436
35:45.404 --> 35:47.510
Have a good day.

437
35:48.168 --> 35:52.321
Ms. Geum, this is exactly why I said this won't work.

438
35:52.321 --> 35:55.759
I need to get my nails done. What a waste of time.

439
35:56.700 --> 35:57.971
I don't get it.

440
35:57.971 --> 35:59.773
Them and their "global" this and "Korean wave" that.

441
35:59.773 --> 36:04.144
How are rookies supposed to grow if all they want are already acclaimed actors?

442
36:04.144 --> 36:08.273
You'd think those people were born as global stars.

443
36:08.273 --> 36:10.339
Whatever, I don't want to work with you.

444
36:10.993 --> 36:12.364
Just you wait.

445
36:12.364 --> 36:16.338
Everyone will be lining up for a chance to cast Ha Na soon enough.

446
36:35.840 --> 36:36.843
[My Star]

447
36:40.286 --> 36:43.723
[My Boss]

448
36:43.723 --> 36:46.500
The person you are calling is unavailable...

449
36:46.500 --> 36:48.007
[My Star]

450
36:55.120 --> 36:57.307
[What are you doing tonight? Busy?] [I'm waiting for the director and writer now]

451
37:00.614 --> 37:03.198
You're twinkling so bright,

452
37:05.607 --> 37:08.348
but you're too far away to hold on to.

453
37:10.747 --> 37:13.925
So who is this Park Gi Tae guy?

454
37:25.127 --> 37:27.094
[Lee Hyeong Won]

455
37:27.094 --> 37:30.442
The day I got my first gold medal as a judo player,

456
37:34.227 --> 37:37.270
- he said he didn't like seeing me win. - Let go of me!

457
37:39.474 --> 37:41.567
He wanted to stop me from playing ever again.

458
37:41.567 --> 37:43.680
So he slit my wrist.

459
37:43.680 --> 37:45.380
Evil incarnate.

460
38:03.767 --> 38:07.092
Do you know where he is now?

461
38:08.867 --> 38:10.275
No, I don't.

462
38:11.674 --> 38:13.398
You don't?

463
38:13.398 --> 38:16.288
He left the orphanage as soon as he became an adult,

464
38:16.288 --> 38:19.332
but it's pretty obvious where troubled kids like him would end up.

465
38:23.514 --> 38:25.111
Where?

466
38:25.111 --> 38:28.914
Somewhere you can get paid to do illegal things.

467
38:30.314 --> 38:32.014
Which is exactly...

468
38:32.660 --> 38:34.360
what led him back to me.

469
38:45.323 --> 38:49.327
We ran the license plate, and sure enough, the bike was registered as stolen.

470
38:49.327 --> 38:53.912
We'll secure the security footage and track him down.

471
38:59.528 --> 39:01.436
I did some digging on his peers from the orphanage,

472
39:01.436 --> 39:04.740
and on illegal motorcycle dealers as well,

473
39:04.740 --> 39:06.639
but there's no trace of him.

474
39:07.228 --> 39:08.956
This was a planned disappearance.

475
39:08.956 --> 39:12.711
Nobody, not even me, will ever find this guy.

476
39:16.526 --> 39:18.226
[Detective Gonan] [Simple to hire, results sure as fire!]

477
39:20.846 --> 39:22.986
He seems like a weirdo.

478
39:22.986 --> 39:24.303
Really?

479
39:24.303 --> 39:26.250
But I heard he's really famous.

480
39:26.250 --> 39:27.656
[Detective Gonan]

481
39:34.627 --> 39:36.160
[Soo Hyuk]

482
39:38.290 --> 39:39.587
Yes, Soo Hyuk?

483
39:39.587 --> 39:41.763
Woo Jae! Where are you?

484
39:41.763 --> 39:43.829
I just have someone to meet before I go home.

485
39:43.829 --> 39:46.136
I'll make sure it doesn't interfere with tomorrow's schedule.

486
39:46.136 --> 39:48.070
Okay, then.

487
39:48.070 --> 39:50.140
Good job today.

488
39:50.140 --> 39:51.840
Thank you.

489
40:30.323 --> 40:31.771
Woo Jae.

490
40:35.430 --> 40:37.130
Yes, Director?

491
40:37.790 --> 40:41.029
Did you know you've never called me "bro?"

492
40:42.730 --> 40:44.226
I'm...

493
40:45.965 --> 40:47.829
only staying in my lane.

494
40:51.550 --> 40:53.093
Woo Jae.

495
40:53.716 --> 40:55.727
Stay in your lane.

496
40:58.021 --> 40:59.485
I see.

497
41:01.906 --> 41:05.150
Stop wasting time and say what you want to say.

498
41:05.150 --> 41:09.077
What's this about Ha Na quitting acting?

499
41:09.713 --> 41:12.993
Of course she didn't tell you.

500
41:14.726 --> 41:16.426
Woo Jae, you...

501
41:17.093 --> 41:19.744
Do you know anything about Ha Na's camcorder?

502
41:34.966 --> 41:36.666
What... is this?

503
41:39.438 --> 41:42.564
Year... 2026?

504
41:52.756 --> 41:55.750
That's sudden. A camcorder?

505
41:56.436 --> 41:57.747
What's this about?

506
41:58.990 --> 42:02.187
In my opinion, Ha Na and her twin brother...

507
42:02.187 --> 42:04.098
How do I put this...

508
42:04.098 --> 42:06.170
They seem like different beings.

509
42:07.390 --> 42:09.260
Didn't you feel it, too?

510
42:09.260 --> 42:11.688
You're the person closest to them.

511
42:14.096 --> 42:16.239
I wish you'd start making some sense.

512
42:23.370 --> 42:26.142
I think the twins came from the future.

513
42:27.663 --> 42:31.096
Yang Jun Mo is the stalker...

514
42:31.096 --> 42:33.240
Then what's the deal with Lee Hyeong Won?

515
42:33.240 --> 42:35.324
What do they have to do with each other?

516
42:35.324 --> 42:38.882
Besides, didn't he originally disappear during sophomore year?

517
42:38.882 --> 42:40.950
What could this mean?

518
42:40.950 --> 42:43.247
Why would they gang up on not only you,

519
42:43.247 --> 42:46.348
but Woo Jae as well? There's no reason to!

520
42:46.348 --> 42:48.072
You know, I...

521
42:48.072 --> 42:51.035
I hope you live a happy life, Woo Jae.

522
42:51.035 --> 42:53.578
And a long one at that.

523
42:55.442 --> 42:58.448
If you're just going to sit there spouting nonsense,

524
42:58.448 --> 43:01.507
- I'll see myself out. - What if it's because of you?

525
43:05.088 --> 43:07.655
What if the camcorder is a time machine?

526
43:08.328 --> 43:12.126
What if Ha Na traveled back in time to save you?

527
43:12.126 --> 43:14.570
If not, why would she suddenly announce that she's giving up acting?

528
43:14.570 --> 43:16.451
It was her lifelong dream.

529
43:16.451 --> 43:20.231
We don't know what happens in the future.

530
43:20.231 --> 43:22.302
But one thing's for sure.

531
43:22.302 --> 43:24.406
You die in the future,

532
43:24.406 --> 43:29.169
and Ha Na, in an attempt to save you, ends up giving up on her dream.

533
43:36.148 --> 43:39.421
Are you sure you're in your right mind?

534
43:40.035 --> 43:42.615
That just doesn't make any sense...

535
43:43.475 --> 43:45.188
Do you really think so?

536
43:45.188 --> 43:47.115
That it doesn't make any sense?

537
43:48.975 --> 43:50.675
You know, Yoon Ha Ru...

538
43:51.295 --> 43:55.399
He was a judo prodigy, but ended up quitting due to an injury, right?

539
43:55.399 --> 43:57.943
Don't you think that's also because of you?

540
43:57.943 --> 44:02.140
He traveled back in time to save you and got his life screwed over.

541
44:03.708 --> 44:05.178
You!

542
44:06.348 --> 44:08.048
Stay away!

543
44:14.295 --> 44:17.759
The twins have thrown everything away just to save your life,

544
44:17.759 --> 44:19.330
but you?

545
44:19.330 --> 44:22.300
Don't you want to protect their lives as well?

546
44:22.300 --> 44:24.309
What's your point?

547
44:28.055 --> 44:29.855
The camcorder.

548
44:29.855 --> 44:33.035
They will give everything up for you, here, in the past.

549
44:33.035 --> 44:34.907
So we should get rid of it.

550
44:37.715 --> 44:40.179
It still makes no sense,

551
44:40.179 --> 44:41.830
but even if it did...

552
44:41.830 --> 44:44.708
What does this have to do with you?

553
44:44.708 --> 44:46.632
I want to protect Ha Na's life.

554
44:46.632 --> 44:49.555
I don't want to lose such a great actress.

555
44:49.555 --> 44:51.375
Woo Jae, I...

556
44:51.375 --> 44:54.316
I want Ha Na to live her dream.

557
44:55.175 --> 44:56.628
Don't you?

558
44:57.608 --> 44:58.960
You.

559
44:59.982 --> 45:03.790
Are you sure you can handle watching their lives fall into misery just for you?

560
45:04.535 --> 45:06.342
I know you're not.

561
45:06.342 --> 45:09.042
We may have our differences, you and I,

562
45:09.628 --> 45:11.573
but we serve the same purpose.

563
45:12.582 --> 45:14.165
To protect Ha Na.

564
45:23.942 --> 45:26.066
We may have our differences, you and I,

565
45:26.066 --> 45:27.630
but we serve the same purpose.

566
45:27.630 --> 45:29.330
To protect Ha Na.

567
45:30.142 --> 45:32.068
No!

568
45:34.068 --> 45:35.752
Woo Jae...

569
45:35.752 --> 45:37.288
I have to go now.

570
45:37.288 --> 45:39.679
- To where? - I don't know.

571
45:39.679 --> 45:41.592
But when I do...

572
45:42.316 --> 45:44.715
I might never see you again.

573
46:02.242 --> 46:03.698
Woo Jae!

574
46:10.083 --> 46:13.052
Woo Jae. Is there something wrong?

575
46:13.052 --> 46:15.018
I missed you so much.

576
46:16.358 --> 46:18.148
You're silly.

577
46:18.148 --> 46:19.620
Me too.

578
47:01.808 --> 47:04.159
Jung Woo Jae, you...

579
47:04.159 --> 47:06.350
feel different today.

580
47:23.887 --> 47:25.410
I love you.

581
47:32.081 --> 47:33.676
Me too.

582
48:26.356 --> 48:28.643
[Happy Home]

583
49:01.129 --> 49:02.829
Did you sleep well?

584
49:05.972 --> 49:09.096
What's all this? Jung Woo Jae!

585
49:14.393 --> 49:16.728
Cute.

586
49:16.728 --> 49:18.974
Hey, new guy, close your eyes!

587
49:20.465 --> 49:22.342
- Yes, sir! - Woo Jae.

588
49:22.342 --> 49:24.846
This is good. This is all so great,

589
49:24.846 --> 49:28.244
but I have to remind you once more that this is Ye Rang Entertainment's quarters.

590
49:28.244 --> 49:29.781
Yeah, I'm aware.

591
49:29.781 --> 49:32.278
For your information, we'll be coming home late today.

592
49:32.278 --> 49:35.132
And I mean very, very late.

593
49:35.132 --> 49:37.089
So take that into consideration.

594
49:37.089 --> 49:39.234
Yeah, me too.

595
49:41.891 --> 49:43.890
- Let's go. - Go, go!

596
49:44.491 --> 49:46.868
- May I open my eyes now? - Yeah, come on! Let's go.

597
49:46.868 --> 49:49.518
- Let's go! - Yes, sir!

598
50:16.327 --> 50:18.624
What's all this?

599
50:33.138 --> 50:35.691
I'm sorry you had to see that first thing in the morning, Seok Min.

600
50:35.691 --> 50:37.104
No, no.

601
50:37.104 --> 50:39.044
I didn't see anything!

602
50:39.044 --> 50:41.133
Hey, Ha Ru?

603
50:43.106 --> 50:49.419
I've been contemplating whether I should tell you or not...

604
50:49.419 --> 50:50.784
What is it?

605
51:08.031 --> 51:11.003
How did you even come up with all this?

606
51:12.344 --> 51:14.624
You said you wanted a day to empty your brain

607
51:14.624 --> 51:17.582
and watch all your favorite movies until you got sick of them.

608
51:17.582 --> 51:20.346
That's your idea of a romantic day, right?

609
51:23.964 --> 51:27.731
No, my idea of a romantic day...

610
51:27.731 --> 51:29.584
is with you, Jung Woo Jae.

611
51:35.011 --> 51:36.858
What?

612
52:04.904 --> 52:06.854
Just until the guys get back home, okay?

613
52:09.351 --> 52:10.836
Okay.

614
52:44.111 --> 52:45.502
Woo Jae.

615
52:47.451 --> 52:50.895
Nothing's wrong, right?

616
52:52.824 --> 52:54.979
Yeah, nothing's wrong.

617
52:56.624 --> 52:58.642
If anything goes wrong,

618
52:58.642 --> 53:00.612
you need to tell me.

619
53:00.612 --> 53:02.648
You don't have to suffer alone.

620
53:05.178 --> 53:06.878
Of course.

621
53:15.724 --> 53:17.120
Ha Na.

622
53:17.778 --> 53:19.011
Yeah?

623
53:21.318 --> 53:25.928
Whatever hardships we go through in the future,

624
53:27.491 --> 53:29.924
we shouldn't give up on our dreams.

625
53:29.924 --> 53:31.523
Never.

626
53:36.598 --> 53:39.343
Why are you bringing up dreams all of a sudden?

627
53:41.524 --> 53:45.162
Aren't you going to answer me?

628
53:49.018 --> 53:50.335
Of course.

629
53:50.335 --> 53:51.826
I won't give up.

630
53:51.826 --> 53:54.509
So you promise?

631
53:56.178 --> 53:57.878
Promise?

632
54:22.631 --> 54:24.175
Welcome, table for how many, sir?

633
54:24.175 --> 54:25.875
I'm here alone.

634
54:33.298 --> 54:36.011
Do you like watching movies?

635
54:36.011 --> 54:37.948
I do like movies.

636
54:37.948 --> 54:39.619
Here's the menu.

637
54:39.619 --> 54:41.284
Take your time browsing through it.

638
54:41.284 --> 54:42.387
Hey, actually...

639
54:42.387 --> 54:45.159
Can I get an iced chocolate, extra sweet?

640
54:45.159 --> 54:47.790
Okay, I'll take the menu away for you.

641
54:47.790 --> 54:50.252
I'd like to browse some more.

642
54:51.071 --> 54:52.771
Right, of course.

643
54:58.278 --> 55:02.824
I started out as an entry-level employee, but climbed the ranks faster than the others.

644
55:02.824 --> 55:05.196
Well, yes, it is my father's company,

645
55:05.196 --> 55:08.554
but I lived a hardworking life, and started at the bottom.

646
55:08.554 --> 55:12.119
I was working while others fooled around.

647
55:13.252 --> 55:14.669
I see.

648
55:20.631 --> 55:23.615
You know, we're four years apart.

649
55:23.615 --> 55:26.064
They say it's the perfect age gap.

650
55:26.064 --> 55:28.422
What a boring pickup line.

651
55:29.291 --> 55:30.991
Is that so?

652
55:32.396 --> 55:33.959
I want to marry fast.

653
55:33.959 --> 55:37.946
I want to provide my wife with stability.

654
55:37.946 --> 55:40.435
The outside world is like a war zone.

655
55:40.435 --> 55:43.664
I don't want my beloved to struggle alone.

656
55:43.664 --> 55:48.108
I want to let her rest easy behind the fence that I built.

657
55:51.211 --> 55:53.370
That's a beautiful sentiment.

658
55:55.460 --> 55:57.416
"A beautiful sentiment?"

659
57:29.091 --> 57:30.915
Ms. Ye Rang.

660
57:30.915 --> 57:32.239
Yes?

661
57:32.239 --> 57:34.263
Please think fondly of me.

662
57:34.263 --> 57:36.851
- Pardon me? - Love at first sight...

663
57:36.851 --> 57:38.428
I never believed in it,

664
57:38.428 --> 57:41.652
but having met you today, I do now.

665
57:41.652 --> 57:45.870
I think I'm only going to fall deeper for you.

666
58:15.198 --> 58:16.898
Woo Jae.

667
58:29.698 --> 58:31.398
That bastard!

668
59:21.598 --> 59:23.641
What are you doing, Woo Jae?

669
59:29.571 --> 59:31.528
Are you alright, sir?

670
59:33.345 --> 59:34.728
Sir?

671
59:43.518 --> 59:45.628
- Who, me? - Yes.

672
59:46.798 --> 59:48.785
I'm absolutely fine.

673
59:49.736 --> 59:51.947
Call me if you need anything.

674
59:51.947 --> 59:53.198
Okay.

675
01:00:25.302 --> 01:00:27.826
Why is this here?

676
01:00:32.255 --> 01:00:33.473
Sorry.

677
01:00:33.473 --> 01:00:36.760
I dropped it. I think it broke.

678
01:00:38.642 --> 01:00:42.013
It's okay. It's always been a piece of junk.

679
01:00:42.013 --> 01:00:44.618
It held up for longer than I thought it would.

680
01:01:30.087 --> 01:01:32.953
The contents of the script... changed.

681
01:01:32.953 --> 01:01:35.676
If I can't have you for myself...

682
01:01:35.676 --> 01:01:37.278
The camcorder...

683
01:01:37.278 --> 01:01:39.114
It's gone!

684
01:01:39.114 --> 01:01:41.427
Every action we take

685
01:01:41.427 --> 01:01:43.141
can't be reversed anymore.

686
01:01:43.141 --> 01:01:45.491
Unless you want to ruin what we have left,

687
01:01:45.491 --> 01:01:48.095
at least have some respect.

688
01:01:48.095 --> 01:01:51.066
The reason why you're traveling through time is to save my life,

689
01:01:51.066 --> 01:01:52.790
is that right?

690
01:01:52.790 --> 01:01:54.486
Please, just stop.

691
01:01:54.486 --> 01:01:57.030
The true finale...

692
01:01:57.030 --> 01:01:59.156
is only starting now.
